{
 "source": "geneva",
 "book": "1KI",
 "chapter": 14,
 "units": [
  {
   "id": "geneva/1KI.14.2",
   "range": "1KI.14.2",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "5f4855a9",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/1KI.14.2#p1-5f4855a9",
     "text": "His own conscience bore witness to him that the prophet of God would not satisfy his desires, who was a wicked man.",
     "label": "a",
     "anchor": "and disguise thyself"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/1KI.14.3",
   "range": "1KI.14.3",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "98764e96",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/1KI.14.3#p1-98764e96",
     "text": "According to the custom when they went to ask counsel of prophets, 1Sa 9:7.",
     "label": "b",
     "anchor": "thee ten loaves",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "1Sa 9:7",
       "ref": "1SA.9.7"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/1KI.14.5",
   "range": "1KI.14.5",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "bdfbcce0",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/1KI.14.5#p1-bdfbcce0",
     "text": "Than the wife of Jeroboam.",
     "label": "c",
     "anchor": "another woman"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/1KI.14.6",
   "range": "1KI.14.6",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "05f518d5",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/1KI.14.6#p1-05f518d5",
     "text": "For God often discloses to his own the craft and subtilty of the wicked.",
     "label": "d",
     "anchor": "wife of Jeroboam"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/1KI.14.7",
   "range": "1KI.14.7",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "f5946e8b",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/1KI.14.7#p1-f5946e8b",
     "text": "Who was but a servant.",
     "label": "e",
     "anchor": "thee from among the people"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/1KI.14.9",
   "range": "1KI.14.9",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "27ab2eda",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/1KI.14.9#p1-27ab2eda",
     "text": "That is, two calves.",
     "label": "i",
     "anchor": "molten images"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/1KI.14.10",
   "range": "1KI.14.10",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "828020e1",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/1KI.14.10#p1-33770093",
     "text": "Every male even to the dogs, 1Sa 25:22.",
     "label": "g",
     "anchor": "pisseth against the wall",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "1Sa 25:22",
       "ref": "1SA.25.22"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "geneva/1KI.14.10#p2-d304341a",
     "text": "As well him that is in the stronghold, as him that is abroad.",
     "label": "h",
     "anchor": "is shut up and left in"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/1KI.14.11",
   "range": "1KI.14.11",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "56fe9669",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/1KI.14.11#p1-56fe9669",
     "text": "They will lack the honour of burial in token of God's curse.",
     "label": "i",
     "anchor": "for the LORD hath spoken it"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/1KI.14.13",
   "range": "1KI.14.13",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "118822b8",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/1KI.14.13#p1-118822b8",
     "text": "In the midst of the wicked, God has some on whom he bestows his mercies.",
     "label": "k",
     "anchor": "some good thing toward the LORD"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/1KI.14.14",
   "range": "1KI.14.14",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "78c2530f",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/1KI.14.14#p1-78c2530f",
     "text": "The Lord will begin to destroy it out of hand.",
     "label": "l",
     "anchor": "but what"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/1KI.14.15",
   "range": "1KI.14.15",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "0dca1bf8",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/1KI.14.15#p1-0dca1bf8",
     "text": "Meaning the Euphrates.",
     "label": "m",
     "anchor": "river"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/1KI.14.16",
   "range": "1KI.14.16",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "40782a3b",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/1KI.14.16#p1-40782a3b",
     "text": "The people will not be excused when they do evil at the commandment of their governors.",
     "label": "n",
     "anchor": "made Israel to sin"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/1KI.14.20",
   "range": "1KI.14.20",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "afce5552",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/1KI.14.20#p1-afce5552",
     "text": "The Lord smote him and he died, 2Ch 13:20.",
     "label": "o",
     "anchor": "slept with his fathers",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "2Ch 13:20",
       "ref": "2CH.13.20"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/1KI.14.21",
   "range": "1KI.14.21",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "865a3ae5",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/1KI.14.21#p1-865a3ae5",
     "text": "And died about four years before Jeroboam.",
     "label": "p",
     "anchor": "years in Jerusalem"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/1KI.14.24",
   "range": "1KI.14.24",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "952bd494",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/1KI.14.24#p1-952bd494",
     "text": "Where idolatry reigns, all horrible vices are committed, till at length God's just judgment destroys them completely.",
     "label": "q",
     "anchor": "land"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/1KI.14.29",
   "range": "1KI.14.29",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "454129a9",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/1KI.14.29#p1-454129a9",
     "text": "Which were called the books of Shemaiah and Iddo the prophets, 2Ch 12:15.",
     "label": "r",
     "anchor": "the book of the chronicles of",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "2Ch 12:15",
       "ref": "2CH.12.15"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/1KI.14.30",
   "range": "1KI.14.30",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "ab3ee016",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/1KI.14.30#p1-ab3ee016",
     "text": "That is, all the days of Rehoboam's life.",
     "label": "s",
     "anchor": "all their days"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/1KI.14.31",
   "range": "1KI.14.31",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "9071d3fe",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/1KI.14.31#p1-9071d3fe",
     "text": "Whose idolatry Rehoboam her son followed.",
     "label": "t",
     "anchor": "Ammonitess"
    }
   ]
  }
 ]
}
